\par\par \b \uc2 Latvia  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  reserves up by 10 pct in March\b0\par\par\uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 2010\par 12:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TALLINN, April 7 (Reuters) - Latvia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose by 9.94 percent in February to 5.57 billion euros ($7.44 billion) from 5.01 billion euros in the previous month as the third instalment of rescue package funds were paid to the government.\par \par \uc2 The Latvian lat has moved away from the weak end of its trading band to be close the same level last seen in December last year. The country is still awash with unplaced lats with banks not giving Lat denominated loans and so helping pull down yields on treasury bills, one of the few places to place lats.\par \par \uc2 The Latvian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the increase in the reserves' was "mostly due to the third instalment of the loan received from the European Commission to the amount of 495.2 million euro."\par \par \uc2 The Latvian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  added that it held convertible foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of 5.228 billion euros up from 4.726 billion euros at the end of February.\par \par \uc2 Lithuania's official reserve assets were down by 15.3 percent month on month, or 2.99 billion litas ($1.16 billion) lower at 16.4 billion litas at the end of March.\par \par \uc2 The Lithuanian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the central government's deposits contracted by 2.42 billion litas over the month.\par \par \uc2 Estonia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's official reserve and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets fell by 2.6 percent to 41.7 billion Estonian kroons ($3.56 billion) in March from 42.8 billion kroons at the end of February, the Estonian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on its website on Wednesday.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2  announces its net \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  position after its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  every Monday, including on Reuters page <LVBANK11>.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by David Mardiste; editing by Ron Askew)\par \par \uc2 BALTIC-RESERVES/|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|DA|FN|NW|SW   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100407e647000na\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
