\par\par \b \uc2 Latvian c.bank net  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2  at zero last week\b0\par\par\uc2 348 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2010\par 10:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 RIGA, March 29 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it had a zero net position for \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second week running last week, seen as a signal of easing pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's band against the euro.\par \par \uc2 The lat's trading band come under pressure in 2008 and 2009 during an economic crisis that sent it to the IMF for help, but \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year has been limited or even aimed at capping gains, easing speculation the government would have to devalue.\par \par \uc2 In early trade, the lat <EURLVL=> was little changed from last week, with the euro quoted at 0.7074/84 lats compared with a 0.7075 close on Friday. The lat is still clear of the 0.7098 level at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, one trader saw little chance the lat will appreciate further in its band.\par \par \uc2 "Banks have to make provisions for bad loans and therefore there is demand for euros," said one trader.\par \par \uc2 In Latvia, most loans are issued in euros and banks have to make provisions for bad loans, which have soared in the crisis, in that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  automatically accepts offers to buy lats in what it calls passive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the euro hits 0.7098 lats, the top end of its 1 percent fluctuation band based on a central rate of 0.7028 lats.\par \par \uc2 The trader also noted that Latvian banks have started using a new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  7-day deposit facility, placing 397.2 million lats on March 26.\par \par \uc2 "That means that liquidity is still high and there is a surplus of lats in the market," said the trader.\par \par \uc2 The bank set an an interest rate of 1 percent on the facility, introduced to make liquidity more predictable.\par \par \uc2 Markets have remained calm in recent weeks despite the withdrawal of the largest party from the government, turning it into a minority administration.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Aija Braslina; editing by Patrick Graham)\par \par \uc2 LATVIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100329e63t000gw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
