\par\par \b \uc2 Latvian c.bank says no net  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2  last week\b0\par\par\uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2010\par 10:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 RIGA, March 22 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it ended last week with balanced net \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and dealers said local markets remained calm despite political ups and downs.\par \par \uc2 The bank, which reports its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a Monday for the previous week, made net purchases of 45 million euros two weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 In early trade, the lat <EURLVL=> was a touch weaker, with the euro quoted at 0.7072/87 lats after ending Friday at 0.7074/84, though it was still clear of the 0.7098 level at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Events on the political stage have not affected the market as there are plenty of lats," said one trader.\par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Valdis Dombrovskis has been left with a minority government after the largest coalition party quit the government last week.\par \par \uc2 Dombrovskis is to hold talks this week with an opposition party as he seeks to rebuild his parliamentary majority.\par \par \uc2 The local financial market has taken the political shifts in its stride, banking that even if the opposition does not join the government it will not undermine Latvia's bailout programme with the International Monetary Fund and European Union.\par \par \uc2 Ratings agency \uc2 Moody's\uc2  said last week that Latvia had greater financial buffers now than a year ago and also that Dombrovskis did not face any big political decisions ahead of an Oct. 2 election that would be crucial for the bailout.\par \par \uc2 The trader said demand for euros could rise with the approach of the end of the month, when banks often tackle provisioning for bad loans, which has to be done in euros. This could drive the lat back up to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  automatically accepts offers to buy lats in what it calls passive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the euro hits 0.7098 lats, the top end of its 1 percent fluctuation band based on a central rate of 0.7028 lats. (Reporting by Aija Braslina, editing by Mike Peacock)\par \par \uc2 LATVIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|DA|FN|NW|SW   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100322e63m000js\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
