\par\par \b \uc2 Latvia  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  reserves rise in Jan\b0\par\par\uc2 281 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 2010\par 12:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TALLINN, Feb 5 (Reuters) - Latvia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose by 2.2 percent in January to 4.9 billion euros ($6.72 billion) on the back of government deposits.\par \par \uc2 Latvia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has remained close to the weak end of its trading band with the euro with the local money market awash with lats, but with limited opportunies for banks to invest in the local market.\par \par \uc2 The bank said the increase in the reserves' was "due to the expansion of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds deposits by the Latvian Government".\par \par \uc2 It added it held convertible foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of 4.584 billion euros up from 4.484 billion euros at the end of December.\par \par \uc2 Latvia was the worst hit of the European Union's three small Baltic states in the financial crisis, forced to reach out to the IMF for support as it bid to keep its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg to the euro unchanged. Lithuania and Estonia have followed similar paths, although their decline has been less steep.\par \par \uc2 Lithuania's reserves rose by 2.8 percent from a month ago to 16.5 billion litas ($6.56 billion), the Lithuanian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Estonia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets fell by 2.2 percent to 41.1 billion kroons ($3.60 billion) in January from the end of December, data on the Estonian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's website showed.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2  announces its net position after its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  every Monday, including on Reuters page <LVBANK11>.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by David Mardiste; editing by Patrick Graham)\par \par \uc2 BALTIC-RESERVES/|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100205e625001op\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
