\par\par \b \uc2 Latvia c.bank bought 19 mln euros last week\b0\par\par\uc2 347 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2010\par 10:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 RIGA, Jan 4 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week led to a net purchase of 19 million euros, down from net euro purchases of 45 million euros two weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 In early trade on Monday, the lat <EURLVL=> was slightly firmer, with the euro quoted at 0.7086/96 lats versus 0.7083/98 lats the Wednesday before the New Year holidays.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  automatically accepts offers to buy lats in what it calls passive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the euro hits 0.7098 lats, the top end of its 1 percent fluctuation band based on a central rate of 0.7028 lats.\par \par \uc2 "The positive position was due most likely to Latvian state treasury \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as it must convert euros for lats via the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as part of the agreement with the IMF, while the market was opposite, with the lat at the weak end of its trading band," one trader said.\par \par \uc2 Traders expected a quiet week with little pressure on the lat and maybe some clients buying lats while it was weaker against the euro. They saw little speculative pressure.\par \par \uc2 The main cloud on the horizon is the hitch in talks with the International Monetary Fund and the European Union after a constitutional court ruling that plans to cut pensions were illegal.\par \par \uc2 This means the government needs to find a further 100 million lats in the budget this year, either from spending cuts, revenue rises or letting the budget deficit rise.\par \par \uc2 Any of these measures have to coordinated with the lenders, the government has said. Latvia at the end of 2008 struck a deal for a 7.5 billion euro international bailout, led by the IMF and EU and its fiscal policy has to be agreed with the lenders.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announces its net \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the previous week on Mondays, including on the <LVBANK11> Reuters page. (Reporting by David Mardiste, editing by Mike Peacock)\par \par \uc2 LATVIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|DA|FN|NW|SW   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100107e614000jy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
