\par\par \b \uc2 Latvia c.bank reserves rise, Lithuania's fall in Nov\b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2009\par 12:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 RIGA, Dec 7 (Reuters) - The Latvian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose 6.2 percent in November to 4.804 billion euros ($7.15 billion) from 4.523 billion euros in the previous month, it said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 For most of November, Latvia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at the weak end of its band with the euro in thin trade on concerns that the country's 2010 budget cuts may not be approved by parliament and the IMF. By the end of the month, confidence and liquidity recovered with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firming slightly and the budget winning parliamentary approval.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it held convertible foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of 4.479 billion euros, up from 4.218 billion euros at the end of October.\par \par \uc2 Lithuania's reserves fell by 6.15 percent in November to 18.3 billion litas ($7.89 billion) from 19.5 million litas in October, the Lithuanian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said also on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The bank said its reserves shrank due to a fall of 937.9 million litas in central government deposits and a decrease of 388 million litas in Lithuania's external liabilities.\par \par \uc2 Estonia's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gold reserves backing the Estonian kroon firmed by 8.0 percent in November to 40.4 billion kroons ($3.89 bln), up from 37.4 billion kroons at the end of October, its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement on Monday.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2  announces how much it has spent on passive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market every Monday, including on Reuters page <LVBANK11>. In the last week, the Latvian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought 105 million euros and sold lats. (Reporting by David Mardiste; Editing by Victoria Main)\par \par \uc2 BALTIC-RESERVES/|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|DA|FN|NW|SW   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091207e5c7000jb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
