\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Latvia \highlight\uc2  lat steady, cbank did not  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  last wk\b0\par\par\uc2 390 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2009\par 09:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 RIGA, Nov 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it did not make any \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second week running last week with liquidity up and fewer worries over the passing the 2010 budget on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 In early trade on Monday, the lat <EURLVL=> was slightly weaker, but still below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level at 0.7080/95 lats compared to 0.7081/91 lats last Monday.\par \par \uc2 "The situation in the market is calm with a surplus of short-term money and there is the expectation that the 2010 budget's second reading tomorrow will not be a problem," one trader said.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the government appears to have accepted what it must do for the budget and although they do not like it, the government understands that it will have to pass the budget to keep the International Monetary Fund (IMF) and international lenders on side to support a 7.5 billion euro ($11.3 bln) rescue package the country needs.\par \par \uc2 In the week before last, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said that it made no \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, and earlier in November the only trade the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was doing was converting funds for the government treasury's requirements as required by their agreement with the IMF.\par \par \uc2 Liquidity has improved over the last two last weeks with yields on Latvia's domestic borrowing falling by more than one percent and with more participants bidding making the weekly auctions heavily over-subscribed.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  automatically accepts offers to buy lats when the euro hits 0.7098 lats, the top end of its 1 percent fluctuation band based on a central rate of 0.7028 lats.\par \par \uc2 Latvia relies on 7.5 billion euro international monetary fund (IMF) rescue package to keep its finances afloat, but the country's fiscal policy must meet IMF and European Commission approval before more payments from the loan are disbursed.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announces \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday for the previous week, including on the <LVBANK11> Reuters page. ($1=.6640 Euro) (Reporting by David Mardiste, Editing by Toby Chopra) ((via Tallinn newsroom, david.mardiste@thomsonreuters.com Reuters Messaging: david.mardiste.reuters.com@reuters.net))\par \par \uc2 LATVIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|DA|FN|NW|SW   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091203e5bu000gj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
