\par\par \b \uc2 Latvia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves ease, Lithuania's up in Oct\b0\par\par\uc2 288 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 2009\par 11:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 RIGA, Nov 7 (Reuters) - Latvia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell 1.2 percent in October, while Lithuania's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said its reserves grew sharply.\par \par \uc2 Latvia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been trading at the weak end of its band with the euro in recent weeks on concerns the International Monetary Fund may not approve the government's 2010 budget cuts and on the risk of political instability.\par \par \uc2 Its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said reserves slipped to 4.523 billion euros ($6.82 billion) from 4.577 billion euros in September. It said it held convertible foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of 4.218 billion euros, slightly down from 4.277 billion euros at the end of September.\par \par \uc2 Lithuania's reserves increased by 22.7 percent in October to 19.5 billion litas ($8.37 billion) from 15.9 million litas in September, its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The bank said the reserves were boosted by the central government's deposit of 2.7 billion litas after a successful bond issue during the month.\par \par \uc2 Estonia's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gold reserves backing the Estonian kroon eased just 0.1 percent in October to 37.4 billion kroons ($3.55 bln), down from 37.39 billion kroons at the end of September, the Estonian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement on Friday.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2  announces how much it has spent on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market every Monday, including on Reuters page <LVBANK11>. In the last week the Latvian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 16.7 million euros and bought lats.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by David Mardiste; Editing by Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \uc2 BALTIC-RESERVES/|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|DA|FN|NW|SW   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091106e5b6001lo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
