\par\par \b \uc2 Latvia  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  dips, eyes on budget, govt tensions\b0\par\par\uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Oktober 2009\par 10:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  RIGA, Oct 23 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lat weakened again to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level on Friday with the market remaining focussed on the coalition government's efforts to draw up the 2010 budget and any signs of further political tensions.\par \par \uc2  One trader said the suspension on Thursday of the head of the tax office by the finance minister, portrayed in Latvian media as a source of tension within the ruling coalition or even a reason for it to fall, could show up eventually in longer-term lending rates.\par \par \uc2  The euro <EURLVL=> was last quoted at 0.7078/98 lats after being earlier at 0.7082/97 lats. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  automatically takes offers to buy lats when the euro reaches 0.7098 lats in what it calls passive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  "There is not much more activity than usual (in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market). Most money market activity is still in the week and month duration due to continued uncertainty," said another dealer.\par \par \uc2  He said the uncertainty came from the government's drawing up of the 2010 budget and whether it would be enough to meet the terms of the international rescue programme as well as from the political situation within the ruling coalition.\par \par \uc2  The clash between Finance Minister Einars Repse and Tax Office chief Dzintars Jakans has been brewing for weeks and Repse on Thursday suspended Jakans.\par \par \uc2  Latvian media speculated that this could lead to tensions between the New Era party to which Repse belongs and the largest coalition party, the People's Party.\par \par \uc2  However, People's Party chairman, and the justice minister, Marek Seglins, played down such an idea.\par \par \uc2  Asked during a morning radio interview whether the tax office clash would lead to the falling of the government, Seglins said: "I don't think so...I hope not."\par \par \uc2  He said now was a time of great responsibility and the finance minister should focus on the 2010 budget.  (Reporting by Patrick Lannin; editing by Patrick Graham)  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATVIA/|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091023e5an000ql\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
