\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Swedbank says mortgage plan threatens Latvia ops\b0\par\par\uc2 749 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Oktober 2009\par 12:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Would review Latvian \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  if mortgage plan passed\par \par \uc2 * Banks to meet Latvian prime minister next week\par \par \uc2 * Swedbank has $3.4 bln exposure to Latvian mortgage market\par \par \uc2 * Swedbank shares rise on Nordea merger speculation\par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes from Latvian commercial bank association)\par \par \uc2 STOCKHOLM/RIGA, Oct 12 (Reuters) - Swedbank said on Monday it would review its business in Latvia if a controversial mortgage plan went through, and banks said they would meet the country's prime minister next week to discuss the issue.\par \par \uc2 Latvia's Prime Minister, Valdis Dombrovskis, angered banks last week with his surprise proposal. [ID:nL8188838]\par \par \uc2 He said he wanted to limit what banks can collect from defaulted home loan takers to the collateral, which would cause banks' bad debt losses to soar as many property values have slumped below the value of the debts used to purchase them.\par \par \uc2 "If this runs through we need to reconsider our \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Latvia," said Thomas Backteman, vice president of corporate communications for Swedbank, the largest bank in Latvia and the one most exposed to the harsh recession in the Baltic states.\par \par \uc2 He said he did not believe the proposal would fly, but that the bank was closely monitoring the situation.\par \par \uc2 Passing the proposal would increase political risk and make it difficult to work in a situation when a government decides legal issues retroactively. "That's very far from the established legal practice in the EU," he said.\par \par \uc2 He said banks would meet the prime minister on Oct. 22.\par \par \uc2 This was seconded by the head of the Association of Latvian Commercial Banks.\par \par \uc2 "We will give our arguments that this idea is absurd and without any base and is against Latvian civil law," association head Teodors Tverijons told Reuters. If it was carried out, it would lead to sharp reductions in crediting from banks.\par \par \uc2 The banks would also meet European Economic and Monetary Affairs Commissioner Joaquin Almunia, who is visiting Latvia on Tuesday to push Latvia to live up to promises to slash its 2010 budget deficit. "We cannot keep quiet about this," he said.\par \par \uc2 Though Latvia's woes have overshadowed Swedbank recently, its shares got a lift after a report that a possible tie up with largest Nordic bank Nordea could be in the pipes.\par \par \uc2 by 1426 GMT, Swedbank shares were up 5.5 percent. "It's partly the rumours about a merger with Nordea and the fact the bank is threatening to downsize in Latvia," said a trader.\par \par \uc2 Swedish daily Dagens Nyheter said a possible merger between Swedbank and Nordea was being evaluated by Nordea's largest shareholder, Sampo.\par \par \uc2 Sampo and Swedbank declined to comment on the matter.\par \par \uc2 EXPOSURE\par \par \uc2 Analysts have said the reform would effectively mean people could walk away from their debts and leave their properties in the hands of the bank.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts have also seen a devaluation risk in the proposal as it would cap home owners' losses, most of whom have loans in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dombrovskis has denied any link with devaluation in his proposal. \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market last week. It said on Monday it sold 15 million euros and bought lats amid controversy over the country's 2010 budget plans. [ID:nC2041]\par \par \uc2 The lat was slightly firmer in late trade after the government earlier promised to make the budget adjustments that international lenders want it to carry out.\par \par \uc2 Backteman said Swedbank had a "substantial" exposure to the Latvian mortgage market. Out of a total of some 61 billion crowns ($8.7 billion) of exposure to Latvia, 24 billion crowns came from mortgage loans, he said.\par \par \uc2 Latvia's bank sector is led by Swedbank , SEB , Nordea and DNB Nord , which are already facing big losses in a real estate crash.\par \par \uc2 Nordea said its total lending in Latvia is about 3.1 billion euros ($4.56 billion), of which 1.1 billion was housing loans.\par \par \uc2 SEB said the impact on it was restricted as lending in Latvia was 3 percent of total loans to corporates and homes.\par \par \uc2 It said lending to corporates and households in Latvia was 40 billion crowns, of which 11 billion crowns was mortgages. SEB said it was also planning to participate in the meeting next week. (Additional reporting by Brett Young in Helsinki; Editing by John Stonestreet and Andrew Macdonald) ($1=7.037 Swedish Crown) ($1=.6795 Euro)\par \par \uc2 SWEDBANK/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|DA|FN|NW|SW|RNP    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091012e5ac0016x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
