\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Latvian lat fears back in focus on loan wrangles\b0\par\par\uc2 693 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2009\par 12:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2  lat at c.bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level, volumes low\par \par \uc2 * Baltic state back in focus due budget, loan wrangles\par \par \uc2 * Fitch affirms rating, sees downgrade if IMF/EU programme\par \par \uc2 unravels\par \par \uc2 * Latvian prime minister criticises Swedish finance minister\par \par \uc2 as aggressive, plays down budget worries (Adds analysts, Fitch, prime minister)\par \par \uc2 By Patrick Lannin\par \par \uc2 RIGA, Oct 6 (Reuters) - The Latvian lat fell to the weak end of its pegged band against the euro on Tuesday after worries over devaluation and hitches in talks with international lenders re-emerged, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 However, analysts disagreed about devaluation chances and the extent of the budget worries and the prime minister was quoted as reiterating he thought his country was making enough of an effort to meet the terms of its 7.5 billion euro rescue.\par \par \uc2 By 1301 GMT, the euro <EURLVL=> was quoted at 0.7078/98 lats, the top end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 1 percent fluctuation band of the euro against the lat. Overnight rates <LVLF=> remained low, though, at 0.50/1.10 percent.\par \par \uc2 "All the comments from Sweden/IMF/EU have led to more pressure. Euro and lat spot is firmly on the top now and all the customers are getting more and more worried," said one trader.\par \par \uc2 Another said that with the lat just sitting at the top of the band, rather than going through it, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might not have to carry out what it calls its passive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The lat is pegged to the euro at a central rate of 0.7028 lats, with a 1 percent fluctuation band.\par \par \uc2 Latvia has strongly rejected any idea it should devalue and said this would not help its economic recovery. But some economists see it likely if Latvia hits problems with lenders.\par \par \uc2 "I still wouldn't rule out the possibility of Latvia being pushed into some forced \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  adjustment. I'm not sure if it wil be a whole-hearted devaluation or a depegging," said RBC strategist Nigel Rendall.\par \par \uc2 He said Latvia's proposed budget cuts to meet 2010 budget goals under the 7.5 billion euro rescue led by the International Monetary Fund (IMF) and European Union (EU) were not enough as new revenues would not be able to fill the funding gap.\par \par \uc2 But Nordea Markets analyst Annika Lindbald wrote in a note that worries about Latvia were overdone, though she also expected more cliff hanger talks with lenders.\par \par \uc2 She said concerns about an imminent collapse "also appear greatly exaggerated" as Latvia was well funded after recent IMF and EU loan disbursements.\par \par \uc2 "Unfortunately Latvia might need to move closer to the prospect of state insolvency again for the 500 million lats of fiscal consolidation measures to be approved," she added.\par \par \uc2 "AGGRESSIVE" SWEDEN\par \par \uc2 The government of Prime Minister Valdis Dombrovskis plans spending cuts of just 225 million lats ($463.6 million), leading to doubts it will meet a promised 500 million lat deficit cut.\par \par \uc2 The government says the planned cuts, some tax rises and carry through from 2009 reductions, will meet the deficit goal.\par \par \uc2 But Swedish Finance Minister Anders Borg, whose government put funds in the rescue deal due to Swedish bank exposure, said at the weekend international patience with Latvia was limited.\par \par \uc2 Dombrovskis, in an interview to Swedish business daily Dagens Industri, hit back. "I have had discussions with the European Commission and IMF representatives and none of them were as aggressive as Mr Borg," he told the newspaper.\par \par \uc2 He also reiterated that currently planned fiscal measures were enough to reach the goals of the loan programme.\par \par \uc2 Ratings agency Fitch affirmed its current BB+ rating on Latvia with a negative outlook, but raised a warning flag.\par \par \uc2 "Failure to implement budget cuts and remain on track with the EU/IMF programme could lead to a downgrade," it said.\par \par \uc2 "A delay to the disbursement of international funds to Latvia would leave fiscal and external financing gaps, undermine confidence and put renewed pressure on the exchange rate." (Reporting by Patrick Lannin; editing by Chris Pizzey)\par \par \uc2 LATVIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|DA|FN|NW|SW|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091006e5a6000l6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
