\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Latvia \highlight\uc2  cbank says  \highlight22\uc2 intervened \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market last week\b0\par\par\uc2 326 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 2009\par 08:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  RIGA, Aug 17 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it had sold Latvian lats and bought 70.0 million euros in the last week, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time in a month in the crisis-hit country.\par \par \uc2  Latvia suffered devaluation pressure in late May and early June as the country's political leaders struggled to reach an agreement with the International Monetary Fund and the European Union on further loans to avoid defaulting on its sovereign debt.\par \par \uc2  The lat has been trading stronger against the euro in the last week after the statistics office said on Aug. 10 the economy contracted a less-than-expected 19.6 percent compared with a forecast drop 22 percent.\par \par \uc2  In early trade, the Lat was trading at 0.7005/0.7003 euros <EURLVL=>, compared to the central rate of 0.7028 and compared with a trading range of  0.7013/0.7033 the week before.\par \par \uc2  The country expected to face an 18 percent decline in gross domestic product this year and a 4 percent drop in 2010, and is relying on a 7.5 billion euro ($10.77 billion) rescue package arranged by the IMF to keep its economy afloat.\par \par \uc2  Friday's fixing of interbank rates fell with the overnight rate being quoted at 0.98/2.38 after hitting highs of 30 percent during the devaluation pressure in late May and early June and down from 1.21/3.27 a week before.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announces its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday for the previous week <LVBANK11>.\par \par \uc2  The pressure is off the lat for the time being, but economists say devaluation fears could re-emerge if the country fails to implement its agreements with the IMF to limit its budget deficit this year and 2010.  (Reporting by David Mardiste; Editing by Kazunori Takada)   \par \par \uc2 LATVIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090817e58h000c2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
