\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED-Latvia lat hits highest in over a year\b0\par\par\uc2 255 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 2009\par 16:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Correct headline to over a year, from two years)\par \par \uc2 LONDON, June 10 (Reuters) - Latvia's lat rose to hit its strongest level against the euro since May 2008 after European Monetary and Economic Affairs Commissioner Joaquin Almunia said the resumption of a delayed IMF-EU aid package would help reassure markets about its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg.\par \par \uc2 The unit was quoted at 0.6965 per euro <EURLVL=>, up 0.4 percent from the previous day but within the 0.6958 upper end of its trading band against the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Overnight rates in \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2  are at a record high after a wave of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within its 1 percent fluctuation band to the euro.\par \par \uc2 Speaking in Brussels, Alumnia said Latvia should continue to cut its budget by 500 million lats next year as alternatives to reducing government spending to cope with its steep recession would be more painful. [ID:nBRU009416]\par \par \uc2 Latvian Prime Minister Valdis Dombrovskis is in Brussels for talks with the European Union (EU) to secure a further 1.2 billion euros of aid from a 7.5 billion-euro loan package led by the International Monetary Fund (IMF).\par \par \uc2 The delay in the disbursement of the deal has rattled investors confidence about the stability of Latvia's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg to the euro. (Reporting by Sebastian Tong; editing by Sujata Rao)\par \par \uc2 LATVIA-CURRRENCY/ (URGENT)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL   \