\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Latvian c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2  jump last week\b0\par\par\uc2 369 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 2009\par 08:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds market rates, dealer quote)\par \par \uc2 RIGA, June 8 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week to support the lat, which has been hit by fears of devaluation, rose to a new high for the year when it sold 237.3 million euros ($331.3 million), the bank said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The bank has now spent 907 million euros this year on supporting the lat. It said last week its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves as of the end of May were 2.97 billion euros.\par \par \uc2 Fears of a devaluation in Latvia due to its double digit percentage fall in economic output caused jitters in eastern European markets and Sweden last week. The lat is pegged to the euro at a central rate with a 1 percent fluctuation band.\par \par \uc2 The bank, which announces \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  every Monday, including on Reuters page <LVBANK11>, sold 134.5 million euros the week before.\par \par \uc2 However, the Latvian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed slightly in early trade on Monday, despite the lingering concerns about a possible devaluation.\par \par \uc2 The lat traded just beyond the level at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support it.\par \par \uc2 By 0649 GMT, the euro was quoted at 0.7075/85. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  benchmark falls where the euro hits 0.7098 lats.\par \par \uc2 "The lat has strengthened a bit already," said Kristaps Strazds, SEB's head of trade and money markets, who expects the lat firming to continue.\par \par \uc2 Another trader said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was continuing to benefit from Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The devaluation fears surrounding the small Baltic state have spilled over into other markets.\par \par \uc2 In Latvia, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support for the lat has drained liquidity from the market and caused interest rates to soar.\par \par \uc2 Interbank market rates, which have also soared to record levels in response to the jitters, were quoted Monday morning at 14.80/19.60 percent.\par \par \uc2 Reuters data showed banks on Monday were offering rates varying from 9.0/14.0 percent or 13/16 percent, though one bank, Nordea, was showing a lat deposit rate of 31.0/34.50 percent. (Reporting by Laura MacInnis and Patrick Lannin; Editing by Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \uc2 LATVIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090611e568000gf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
