\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Latvia c.bank supports lat, rejects devaluation\b0\par\par\uc2 376 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juni 2009\par 08:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief quotes from newspaper)\par \par \uc2 RIGA, June 1 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sharply increased its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week to 134 million euros, but the head of the bank was quoted as again rejecting devaluation.\par \par \uc2 Ilmars Rimsevics said lowering the value of the lat would lead to inflation, a long delay in introducing the euro and a fall in trust in Latvia.\par \par \uc2 Instead, the government had to pursue budget cutting plans to win further lending from the IMF and EU.\par \par \uc2 "A devaluation would lead to the end for many years of the dream of adopting the euro in 2012 or at the latest in 2013," Rimsevics wrote in the Latvijas Avize daily newspaper.\par \par \uc2 The Latvian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement that it spent 134 million euros of reserves to support the lat last week after spending just 1.7 million euros the week before.\par \par \uc2 It was the bank's heaviest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year and brought total 2009 \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to back the lat to 670 million euros.\par \par \uc2 Rimsevics was replying to an article last week by a former prime minister, who called for a 30 percent devaluation in order to boost exports and help Latvia out of its crisis.\par \par \uc2 Fears of a lat devaluation affected markets last week, sending down the Swedish crown and Swedish bank shares due to worries about the Nordic state's exposure to the Baltic region.\par \par \uc2 Rimsevics said supporters of devaluation also favoured paying taxes in euros and a one-sided introduction of the euro, without waiting for formal entry into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  union.\par \par \uc2 "That would lead to an even greater loss of trust to the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the lat, to greater international isolation," he wrote. To avoid this, the government had to stick to its path of cutting spending and get more IMF and EU loans budget.\par \par \uc2 The bank sells euros and buys lats when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits the ceiling of its 1 percent band against a central euro rate.\par \par \uc2 The lat was quoted at 0.7085/97 euros. The top allowed rate is 0.7098 euros. (Reporting by Patrick Lannin and David Mardiste, editing by Mike Peacock)\par \par \uc2 LATVIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090601e561000eg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
