\par\par \b \uc2 Latvia sold 72 mln euros last week to support lat\b0\par\par\uc2 181 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2009\par 09:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 RIGA, March 9 (Reuters) - Latvia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week sold 72 million euros to support the lat \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the bank said on Monday, almost double the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the week before, though the lat has since firmed away from the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the euro reaches 0.7098 lats, the weak end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's one percent fluctuation band. It was at the weak end of the band last week until Tuesday, when it firmed again.\par \par \uc2 The State Treasury last week said it had been converting the 1 billion euros of aid Latvia received from the European Commission, a move which helped the lat to strengthen.\par \par \uc2 In the week of Feb. 23 to Feb. 27 the bank spent 40 million euros to buy lats.\par \par \uc2 By 0820 GMT, the euro was at 0.7070/80 lats <EURLVL=>, meaning it was still clear of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level. (Reporting by Patrick Lannin; editing by David Stamp)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 LATVIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090309e5390012k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
