\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Latvia \highlight\uc2  cbank spent 40 mln eur on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  last wk\b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2009\par 08:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes from trader, details)\par \par \uc2 RIGA, March 2 (Reuters) - Latvia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it spent 40 million euros on buying lats last week, the first time the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has supported the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since it was bailed out by the International Monetary Fund in December.\par \par \uc2 The lat slumped last week after Latvia's government collapsed and \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  downgraded the country's debt rating to junk status, the latest moves in a crisis in which it has already signed up for 7.5 billion euros in IMF aid.\par \par \uc2 In early trade on Monday the lat was still at the weak end of its 1 percent fluctuation band, with the euro being quoted at 0.709/0.71 lats <EURLVL=> by 0845 GMT.\par \par \uc2 "There are still small steady flows selling lats, but no big ticket sales," said one trader, adding that most of the activity was coming from the local banks, indicating retail and small to medium corporate flows.\par \par \uc2 The lat is pegged to the euro at a central rate of 0.7028 lats, with a 1 percent fluctuation band. The bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the euro strengthens to 0.7098, which it did last week.\par \par \uc2 One factor that could support the lat is if the state treasury buys lats with some of the 1 billion euros which Latvia was lent by the European Commission last week.\par \par \uc2 Valdis Dombrovskis, nominated from centre-right opposition party New Era to form a new government, has warned that Latvia faces bankruptcy unless it cuts spending by another 700 million Latvian lats ($1.25 billion). (writing by Nerijus Adomaitis, reporting by Patrick Lannin; editing by Patrick Graham)\par \par \uc2 LATVIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090302e532001b5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
