\par\par \b \uc2 Latvian lat stays at c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  level\b0\par\par\uc2 362 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2009\par 15:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 RIGA, Feb 26 (Reuters) - The Latvian lat <EURLVL=> stayed at the level on Thursday at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support it amid continued economic jitters, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The nervousness is due to worries about the economy, which the Finance Ministry forecasts will shrink 12 percent this year, and political instability after the government fell last Friday.\par \par \uc2 The president earlier named a candidate to form a new government -- former Finance Minister Valdis Dombrovskis of the opposition New Era party.\par \par \uc2 By 1414 GMT, the euro was quoted at 0.7089/99 lats. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the euro hits 0.7098 lats.\par \par \uc2 The bank announces the size of its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Mondays, including on Reuters page <LVBANK11>.\par \par \uc2 "We are firmly on the top (weak end of the band), so most likely again at the end of today some banks will go to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and buy some euros from them," said one trader.\par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  operates what it calls passive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which means it automatically buys lats or sell euros when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits either end of its 1 percent fluctuation band against the euro.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had dipped away from the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level in earlier trade, but by the afternoon had slipped back there.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could get support in coming days if the Treasury converts some of the 1 billion euros sent by the European Commission to Latvia on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The funds were the first part of the EU executive's share of a 7.5 billion euro IMF-led rescue loan Latvia negotiated last year. The Commission has pledged just over 3 billion euros.\par \par \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  this week also downgraded its rating on Latvian debt to junk level, the second EU state rated below investment grade after Romania.\par \par \uc2 Pressure on the lat last year in the run-up to the rescue deal forced the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly to support the lat and keep it within its fluctuation band. (Reporting by Patrick Lannin; Editing by Stephen Nisbet)\par \par \uc2 LATVIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090226e52q001at\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
