\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 1- \highlight22\uc2 Latvia \highlight\uc2  c.bank says may keep  \highlight22\uc2 intervening \highlight\uc2  to back lat   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Jorgen Johansson   \par \uc2 552 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 13:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 RIGA, March 26 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it may have to keep up "passive" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts to support the lat after selling nearly 200 million euros last week.   \par \par \uc2 Surging inflation, fears of economic overheating and rumours of a devaluation have pushed the lat to the bottom end of its permitted trading range against the euro in recent weeks.   \par \par \uc2 On the sidelines of a meeting of euro zone finance ministers in Brussels, Eurogroup Chairman Jean-Claude Juncker said European Union finance chiefs should discuss "all recent developments in the Latvian context".   \par \par \uc2 Latvia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  <LVBANK11> said on Monday it sold a net 195.5 million euros in "passive" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  between March 19 and 25 to support the lat, up from 65 million the prior week.   \par \par \uc2 "I would not be surprised if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  for some time, but we are more than happy to do so,"  \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman Martins Gravitis told Reuters.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets this month for the first time since 2001.   \par \par \uc2 The lat was quoted at 0.7093 at 1600 GMT <EURLVL=> on Monday versus its lowest permitted rate of 0.7098.   \par \par \uc2 Worries about supercharged growth and rising prices led  \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  on Feb. 19 to lower its outlook for Latvia to negative from stable.   \par \par \uc2 Rating agencies have also cited a large current account deficit -- 21 percent of gross domestic product last year -- and strong consumption as signs the economy is growing too fast.   \par \par \uc2 Fitch warned on March 6 that all three Baltic states were in danger of overheating, though it said Latvia faced the biggest risk of a hard landing.   \par \par \uc2 Latvia's gross domestic product grew a record 11.9 percent in 2006 and inflation in February was 7.3 percent, up from 7.1 percent the previous month.   \par \par \uc2 In an effort to rein in growth and inflation, the  \uc2 Bank of Latvia\uc2  on March 15 raised its key interest rate by 50 basis points to 5.5 percent. The government also has announced a proposal to tighten fiscal policy and curb credit growth.   \par \par \uc2 Valery Kargin president of  \uc2 Parex Bank\uc2 , Latvia's second biggest by deposits, told Reuters he had little faith in the government's planned measures.   \par \par \uc2 "I don't think the government's inflation action plan will help to reduce inflation," he said, adding that he held the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  responsible for negative sentiment about the lat.   \par \par \uc2 However, he said he did not think "there will be any devaluation of the lat".   \par \par \uc2 Swift growth and price pressures have dashed Latvia's hopes of joining the euro next year and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Ilmars Rimsevics told Reuters last week 2012 was "the most realistic date" for Latvia to join the euro.   \par \par \uc2 The lat is pegged to the euro under a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board-type system with a central rate of 0.702804 to the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Since April 2005, it has been in the ERM-2 exchange rate mechanism, where the permitted fluctuation band is +/- 15 percent around the agreed central rate. Latvia has unilaterally set a 1 percent fluctuation band.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 LATVIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (WRAPUP 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|DA|FN|NW|SW   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070329e33q0012i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
