\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Latvia c.bank sold 65 mln euros as supported lat  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Patrick Lannin  \par \uc2 478 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 12:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday, further c.bank quotes)  \par \par \uc2 STOCKHOLM, March 19 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it sold 65 million euros last week in "passive" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the lat which remained weak because local banks were rebuilding stocks of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data <LVBANK11> on Monday showed the bank made the sales between March 12 and 18 in its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2001, but a bank spokesman said there was no follow-up action on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said the lat remained weak because domestic banks were rebuilding euro positions depleted after devaluations rumours in mid-February and as foreign bank hedging caused a sharp rise in demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "The Latvian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not been on the market today," said spokesman Martinsh Gravitis.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday and Friday to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has sunk to stay near or at the weakest permitted rate of 0.7098 to the euro in its fluctuation band of 1 percent around a central rate.  \par \par \uc2 The devaluation rumours began to spread on Feb. 16 via mobile phone messages, sending people flocking to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange booths to buy euros and dollars.  \par \par \uc2 In passive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , commercial banks can sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  euros when the lat reaches the lower end of its band, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not go into the market.  \par \par \uc2 The lat was quoted at around 0.7095 to the euro on Monday, still pinned at the weak end of its fluctuation range.  \par \par \uc2 Latvian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief economist Uldis Rutkaste, speaking at a conference on the Baltic state's economy in the Swedish capital, said the lat's continued weakness "largely reflects the fact that domestic banks are trying to rebuild their euro position."  \par \par \uc2 He told Reuters after the seminar that banks had to rebuild stocks after selling \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  to meet residents' demand for euros on the devaluation rumour, and then as foreign banks had hedged their lat positions.  \par \par \uc2 He described the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as small scale.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government have strongly denied any plan to devalue the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Rutkaste said that one of the reasons for Latvia's consumer-led economic boom had been flows of funds to local banks from their foreign parents, Swedish banks SEB and Swedbank.  \par \par \uc2 "The Bank of Latvia's position is that foreign inflows are too high. The domestic economy cannot absorb such high flows," he added.  \par \par \uc2 The bank would be more comfortable if economic growth was 7 to 8 percent rather than the more than 11 percent of 2006.  \par \par \uc2 Swedbank chief executive Jan Liden told the conference that he expected a much lower growth of credit volumes this year.  \par \par \uc2 LATVIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070319e33j000tm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
