\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Latvia \highlight\uc2  lat strong after $15.5mln  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  last wk. \b0\par\par\uc2 379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 2001\par 10:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  RIGA, Nov 20 (Reuters) - The Latvian lat held strong on Tuesday and dealers said they expected it to stay at the top of its trading band until December. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said the Bank of Latvia entered the market last week, buying $15.5 million to keep the lat within its two percent trading band against the SDR basket of world \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 0933 GMT on Tuesday, the lat was dead even with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strongest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level. \par \par \uc2  "It is still near the strongest end of the band and I think it will definitely be there until the end of November," said Leonid Ruderman, head trader with Parex Bank. \par \par \uc2  He said the market expects more demand for lats, against euros, by the finance ministry after the country sold a eurobond of 200 million euro earlier this month. But later on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could slide off the top of the band. \par \par \uc2  "I think in December that the lat may weaken after this selloff (of euros against lats)," Ruderman said. \par \par \uc2  In recent years, December has seen the lat move toward the weaker end of its band due to seasonal pressures. \par \par \uc2  A wide rate differential between the lat and SDR \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  following a string of interest rate cuts by the world's major central banks this year has driven the lat to the top of its band recently, and kept the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market. \par \par \uc2  "Last week we bought approximately $15.5 million," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  portfolio manager Andrejs Viks told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  He said that figure was dominated by one deal but that more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely in the days ahead. \par \par \uc2  "I would say yes there would be something this week or next," he added. \par \par \uc2  On the local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the dollar was 0.6272/77 against the lat, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate was 0.6272/399, where it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within its allowed range. \par \par \uc2  The lat is pegged at 0.7997 to the IMF's world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, the SDR - which includeds the dollar, the yen and other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Latvia engages in passive intevention whenever the lat threatens to break through the limits of its band against the SDR. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011120dxbk02ea8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
