\par\par \b \uc2  Latvian lat flat in trading band, seen steady. \b0\par\par\uc2 393 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 2001\par 09:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  RIGA, July 13 (Reuters) - The Latvian lat held within its recent range against the SDR basket on Friday, and dealers said low activity and an upcoming privatisation would keep it steady to higher in the week ahead. \par \par \uc2  At 0714 the lat was 10 points off its strongest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level, the same level where it traded on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "Not much has changed during the last few days. The lat is 10-12 points above \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the same level," Unibanka \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer Kristaps Strazds said. \par \par \uc2  "There are not very large amounts moving on the interbank market," he added. \par \par \uc2  Dealers have said that the July auction of a two percent stake in Latvian Gas could spur some activity on the interbank market next week or before the settlement date of July 24, otherwise the trading is seen remaining low. \par \par \uc2  The auction would give the state proceeds of at least 2.86 million lats ($4.52 million) if it goes through. \par \par \uc2  "In the last couple of days there has been little change and the situation will continue next week, with the lat possibly strengthening a bit," Vereinsbank \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer Andrejs Greivulis said. \par \par \uc2  At 0714 on the local market, the dollar was 0.6360/65 against the lat, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate was 0.6350/478, where it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within its two percent band against the SDR. \par \par \uc2  The lat has been trading in ranges near the stongest levels it is allowed to hit amid a recent money market squeeze that led the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the week before last, buying $2.5 million. \par \par \uc2  Analysts have blamed a number of factors for the tight liquidity - large issues of government debt, scant funds offered by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid a booming economy and a scramble by commercial banks to finance their reserves amid growth in their sector. \par \par \uc2  They say the country's rising budget deficit is also limiting how much liquidity the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can offer through repurchase auctions and other \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The lat is pegged at 0.7997 to the IMF's world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, the SDR - which includes the dollar, the yen and other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It is allowed to fluctuate in a band of one percent either side. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  engages in passive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever it leaves that range. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx7d03lbz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
