\par\par \b \uc2  Latvian lat 10 pts from  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , seen firming. \b0\par\par\uc2 391 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 2001\par 09:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  RIGA, July 12 (Reuters) - The Latvian lat was stable to firmer within recent ranges against the SDR on Thursday, and dealers said the local unit could strengthen further ahead of a privatisation auction for Latvian Gas next week. \par \par \uc2  At 0728 the lat was 10 points off its strongest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level, slightly firmer than the position of 12 points it held at midday on Wednesday but in very thin trade. \par \par \uc2  "These points (by which the lat has strengthened) are virtual as no large amounts of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been exchanged. Maybe a million or two have been sold on the interbank market, nothing big happened," Hansabanka \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer Sandis Pavlovs said. \par \par \uc2  "In the coming days there will be the Gas auction, and maybe someone could be buying lats," he added. \par \par \uc2  The state will sell its two percent stake in Latvian Gas at a Riga bourse auction on July 19. With the minimum price set at 3.58 lats, the sale would give the state proceeds of at least 2.86 million lats ($4.52 million) if it goes through. \par \par \uc2  The settlement date for the auction is July 24. \par \par \uc2  At 0728 on the local market, the dollar was 0.6352/56 against the lat, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate was 0.6342/470, where it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within its two percent band against the SDR. \par \par \uc2  The lat has been trading in ranges near the stongest levels it is allowed to hit amid a recent money market squeeze that led the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the week before last, buying $2.5 million. \par \par \uc2  Analysts have blamed a number of factors for the tight liquidity - large issues of government debt, scant funds offered by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid a booming economy and a scramble by commercial banks to finance their reserves amid growth in their sector. \par \par \uc2  They say the country's rising budget deficit is also limiting how much liquidity the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can offer through repurchase auctions and other \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The lat is pegged at 0.7997 to the IMF's world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, the SDR - which includes the dollar, the yen and other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It is allowed to fluctuate in a band of one percent either side. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  engages in passive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever it leaves that range. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx7c00g2x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
