\par\par \b \uc2  Latvian lat stuck in range, 12 pts from top. \b0\par\par\uc2 459 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 2001\par 12:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  RIGA, July 11 (Reuters) - The Latvian lat was stuck in its recent ranges within its SDR trading band on Wednesday, despite the temptation of cheap dollars after the greenback's recent slide. \par \par \uc2  At 1013 the lat was 12 points off its strongest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level, basically where it was on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The lat was stable despite the fact the dollar shed over half a percent against the euro and the Swiss frank on Wednesday as turmoil in some emerging markets and weakness in stocks encouraged safe-haven flows into European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The dollar was cheaper but nobody actually wanted to buy it large amounts. Usually when the dollar falls in world markets then there is some interest from bargain hunters to buy dollars on the local market," said Unibanka dealer Kristaps Strazds. \par \par \uc2  At 1013 on the local market, the dollar was 0.6344/49 against the lat, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate was 0.6332/460, where it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within its two percent band against the SDR. \par \par \uc2  There were also further signs that the recent squeeze on money market funds was easing. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Einars Repse said it looked to be tapering off and saw no reason for the Bank of Latvia to increase liquidity on offer. \par \par \uc2  Strazds said Repse's comments were predictable and had no real effect on the market on Wednesday since it sees little room for it to increase liquidity anyway with indications of a rising budget deficit. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, appetite for lats was seen unchanged. \par \par \uc2  "Demand for lats is quite stable these days. Although the money market situation eased a bit there is not any large pressure on the lat at the moment, so it is keeping close to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level," said Strazds. \par \par \uc2  The lat has been trading in ranges near the stongest levels it is allowed to hit amid a recent money market squeeze that led the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the week before last, buying $2.5 million. \par \par \uc2  Analysts have blamed a number of factors for the tight liquidity - large issues of government debt, scant funds offered by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid a booming economy and a scramble by commercial banks to finance their reserves amid growth in their sector. \par \par \uc2  They say the country's rising budget deficit is also limiting how much liquidity the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can offer through repurchase auctions and other \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The lat is pegged at 0.7997 to the IMF's world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, the SDR - which includes the dollar, the yen and other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It is allowed to fluctuate in a band of one percent either side. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  engages in passive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever it leaves that range. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010711dx7b00kzy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
