\par\par \b \uc2  Latvian lat opens unchanged, seen range-bound. \b0\par\par\uc2 379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2001\par 10:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  RIGA, July 10 (Reuters) - The Latvian lat opened unchanged in its trading band on Tuesday and dealers said it would move within recent ranges, with its eyes on the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The lat was 11 points off its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level, unchanged from the position it held early on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "There is not much activity and the market is rather stable. The lat is relatively distanced from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Rates are also decreasing, so the situation with the lat has improved a bit," Vereinsbank \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer Andrejs Greivulis said. \par \par \uc2  "I think it will fluctuate within a range of 20 points off the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for some time. If the dollar strengthens, the lat would strengthen, if the dollar is weaker, the lat will also be weaker," he added. \par \par \uc2  The easing of the dollar since Friday has also helped keep the lat off \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The euro rose to two-week high against the dollar and yen on Tuesday on the back of supportive comments from European officials and better German economic data. \par \par \uc2  At 0814 GMT on the local market, the dollar was 0.6361/66 against the lat, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate was 0.6350/478, where it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within its two percent band against the SDR. \par \par \uc2  The lat has been trading in ranges near the stongest levels it is allowed to hit amid a recent money market squeeze that led the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the week before last, buying $2.5 million. \par \par \uc2  Analysts have blamed a number of factors for the tight liquidity - large issues of government debt, scant funds offered by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid a booming economy and a scramble by commercial banks to finance their reserves amid growth in their sector. \par \par \uc2  They say the country's rising budget deficit is also limiting how much liquidity the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can offer through repurchase auctions and other \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The lat is pegged at 0.7997 to the IMF's world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, the SDR - which includes the dollar, the yen and other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It is allowed to fluctuate in a band of one percent either side. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  engages in passive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever it leaves that range. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010710dx7a00enx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
