\par\par \b \uc2  Latvian lat hovers nine points off  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 476 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 2001\par 11:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  RIGA, June 6 (Reuters) - The Latvian lat hovered nine pips off the top of its band on Friday as dealers watched to see whether sky high rates and a buoyant dollar would push the local unit back into its zone of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar was steady at eight-month highs against the euro and three-month highs against the yen after recent data buoyed confidence in a U.S. economic rebound. \par \par \uc2  A strong dollar usually fuels demand on the local market for lats, which become relatively cheap when the greenback rallies. \par \par \uc2  High local interest rates amid a money market squeeze on funds has also made the lat an attractive buy for strong dollars. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say this will keep the lat in close proximity to its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level - the strongest point in its band before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is drawn automatically into the market - until the market receives a fresh injection of funds, probably through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I guess we should see some good (dollar) amounts flowing into the Bank of Latvia to get fresh lats in circulation, only then. We should see selling into the Bank of Latvia," said Parex Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer Kaspars Punenovs. \par \par \uc2  "So far, as I know, a couple million dollars was sold, it's nothing. We reckon it should be 20-30 million at least to stabilise the situation, to get the rates down." \par \par \uc2  At 0908 GMT on the local market, the dollar was 0.6400/05 against the lat, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate was 0.6391/521, where it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within its two percent band against the SDR. \par \par \uc2  This put the lat nine points off its strongest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level on the bid side, within recent ranges. \par \par \uc2  The recent money market squeeze led the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week, buying $2.5 million. \par \par \uc2  Average offered rates on overnight interbank loans softened by Thursday to 7.64 percent, versus rates of 8.00 percent on Monday and higher at the end of last week. \par \par \uc2  They are still soaring well above their most recent lows of 1.19 percent on March 29. \par \par \uc2  Analysts have blamed a number of factors for the tight liquidity - large issues of government debt, scant funds offered by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid a booming economy and a scramble by commercial banks to finance their reserves amid growth in their sector. \par \par \uc2  They say the country's rising budget deficit is also limiting how much liquidity the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can offer through repurchase auctions and other \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The lat is pegged at 0.7997 to the IMF's world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, the SDR - which includes the dollar, the yen and other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It is allowed to fluctuate in a band of one percent either side. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  engages in passive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever it leaves that range. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010728dx7600qqb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
