\par\par \b \uc2  Latvian lat trades 10 points off  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 464 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 2001\par 09:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  RIGA, June 5 (Reuters) - The Latvian lat was resisting pressure on Thursday from a resurgent dollar, which was pushing the local unit closer to the top of its trading band after it had widened the distance in previous sessions, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In opening trade, the lat was around 10 points from its strongest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after moving as far as 15 by Wednesday's close. \par \par \uc2  A strong dollar usually fuels demand on the local market for lats, which become relatively cheap when the greenback rallies. \par \par \uc2  The dollar made new headway to three-month highs against the yen on Thursday amid bullish sentiment incubated by recent remarks by a senior Japanese financial official. \par \par \uc2  Still, the lat was holding further off the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level - the strongest it is allowed to trade under its two percent band against the IMF's world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, the SDR. \par \par \uc2  It had opened at seven points off on Wednesday, after weakening from around five at Tuesday's midsession. \par \par \uc2  "Partly, perhaps, there is not such a tight situation on the money market as rates eased a bit. But, actually I don't think we will go very far - 20 points maximum," said Unibanka dealer Kristaps Strazds. \par \par \uc2  At 0733 GMT on the local market, the dollar was 0.6393/98 against the lat, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate was 0.6383/512, where it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within its two percent band against the SDR. \par \par \uc2  This put the lat 10 points off its strongest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level on the bid side. \par \par \uc2  The local unit has traded in ranges close to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks amid a liquidity squeeze on the local money market. \par \par \uc2  The squeeze led the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week, buying $2.5 million. \par \par \uc2  Average offered rates on overnight interbank loans softened by Wednesday to 7.81 percent, versus rates of 8.00 percent on Monday and higher at the end of last week. \par \par \uc2  They are still soaring well above their most recent lows of 1.19 percent on March 29. \par \par \uc2  Analysts have blamed a number of factors for the tight liquidity - large issues of government debt, scant funds offered by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid a booming economy and a scramble by commercial banks to finance their reserves amid growth in their sector. \par \par \uc2  They say the country's rising budget deficit is also limiting how much liquidity the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can offer through repurchase auctions and other \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The lat is pegged at 0.7997 to the IMF's world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, the SDR - which includes the dollar, the yen and other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It is allowed to fluctuate in a band of one percent either side. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is drawn into the market automatically whenever it leaves that range. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010912dx75008k0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
