\par\par \b \uc2  Latvian lat eases in range near strong end of band. \b0\par\par\uc2 386 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juli 2001\par 09:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  RIGA, June 4 (Reuters) - The Latvian lat eased within its recent ranges near the top of its trading band early on Wednesday after soaring overnight interest rates deflated, although only slightly, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The situation has not changed very much and it's pretty close to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level, but not that tight," said Janis Strazinskis, senior money market and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer with Vereinsbank Riga. \par \par \uc2  "The lat has been getting less tight in the last few days. Interest rates are not as sky high as they were so the lat is not as close to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Strazinskis added. \par \par \uc2  At 0719 GMT on the local market, the dollar was 0.6368/72 against the lat, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate was 0.6361/489, where it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within its two percent band against the SDR basket. \par \par \uc2  This put the lat seven points off its strongest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level on the bid side, just slightly weaker than its position of five points off early on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The local unit has traded in ranges near here and up to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - the maximum allowable level in its two percent trading band against a basket of world \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  - in recent weeks amid a liquidity squeeze on the local money market. \par \par \uc2  The squeeze led the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week, buying $2.5 million. \par \par \uc2  Average offered rates on overnight interbank loans were at 8.00 percent on Monday, slightly off recent highs but still soaring from their most recent lows of 1.19 percent on March 29. \par \par \uc2  Analysts have blamed a number of factors for the tight liquidity - large issues of government debt, low liquidity offered by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid a booming economy and a scramble by commercial banks to finance their reserves amid growth in their sector. \par \par \uc2  They say the country's rising budget deficit also limits how much liquidity the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can offer through repurchase auctions and other \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The lat is pegged at 0.7997 to the IMF's world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, the SDR - which includes the dollar, the yen and other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It is allowed to fluctuate in a band of one percent either side. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is drawn into the market automatically whenever it leaves that range. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010912dx74007cn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
