\par\par \b \uc2  Latvian lat stuck in range at top of trading band. \b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2001\par 10:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  RIGA, June 3 (Reuters) - The Latvian lat was stuck in ranges near the top of its trading band early on Tuesday - around five points from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and no way down seen for now, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers added that trade had slipped into a summer slump, and low volumes would reinforce the lat's position near the strongest levels permitted under its peg to the SDR basket. \par \par \uc2  "I think for about one month nothing will change. The lat will hang around this range, 10 to 20 points from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Hansabanka dealer Sandris Pavlovs. "I don't expect any big moves." \par \par \uc2  At 0750 GMT on the local market, the dollar was 0.6357/62 against the lat, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate was 0.6352/480, where it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within its two percent band against the SDR basket. \par \par \uc2  This put the lat five points off its strongest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level on the bid side, little changed from its position of three points off at midsession on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The local unit has traded in ranges near here in recent weeks amid a liquidity squeeze on the local money market, which led the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week, buying $2.5 million. \par \par \uc2  Average offered rates on overnight interbank loans were at 8.19 percent on Monday, versus their most recent lows of 1.19 percent on March 29. \par \par \uc2  Analysts have blamed a number of factors for the tight liquidity recently - large issues of government debt, low liquidity offered by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid a booming economy and a scramble by commercial banks to finance their reserves amid growth in their sector. \par \par \uc2  They say the country's rising budget deficit also limits how much liquidity the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can offer through repurchase auctions and other \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The lat is pegged at 0.7997 to the IMF's world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, the SDR - which includes the dollar, the yen and other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It is allowed to fluctuate in a band of one percent either side. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is drawn into the market automatically whenever it leaves that range. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010912dx7300e78\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
