\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Latvia \highlight\uc2  lat opens flat, still close to  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 402 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 2001\par 11:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  RIGA, June 15 (Reuters) - The Latvian lat opened unchanged on Friday after it retreated slightly from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level earlier in the week, but dealers see it holding strong despite recent dollar weakness. \par \par \uc2  At 0852 GMT, the lat was seven points weaker than its strongest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level on the bid side, virtually unchanged from Thursday, when it traded 10 points off the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level. \par \par \uc2  "The lat is still quite strong. Even through the dollar weakened against the euro, there is no high demand for dollars on the local market. That means that the demand for lats remains at a high level," said Unibanka \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer Kristaps Strazds. \par \par \uc2  The euro rose to three week highs against the dollar for the second day on Friday following complaints from U.S. manufacturers about the dollar's strength. \par \par \uc2  The lat neared the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level on Tuesday, trading just two points off, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not yet \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep it within the band, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  It has last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the stronger side of the band on June 5, 1998. \par \par \uc2  "I do not foresee that the lat will waken in the near future, it will hold around the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level. Until the situation with the interest rates and on the interbank market changes, the demand for lats will remain," Strazds said. \par \par \uc2  The average overnight interbank offer rate stood at 7.29 percent on Thursday, up from 7.25 percent on Wednesday and from 5.45 percent a month ago. The rate hit a 19-month high of 7.70 percent on June 7. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the recent liquidity squeeze behind the lat's strength has been caused by financial institutions scrambling for funds to settle T-bill auction purchases as well as state budget expenditures drawing on lat resources. \par \par \uc2  On the local market the dollar was 0.6312/17 against the lat, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate was 0.6305/433, where it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within its two percent band against the SDR basket. \par \par \uc2  The lat is pegged at 0.7997 to the IMF's SDR world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket - which includes the dollar, the yen and other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It is allowed to fluctuate in a band of one percent either side. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is drawn into the market automatically whenever it leaves that range. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6f01mjr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
