\par\par \b \uc2  Latvian lat stuck in recent range vs SDR basket. \b0\par\par\uc2 319 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2000\par 10:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par RIGA, May 12 (Reuters) - The Latvian lat\tab   remained\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stuck in its recent range against the SDR basket early on Friday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  and dealers said calm trade would keep it in a tight band \par \par \uc2  throughout the day. \par \par \uc2  At 0830 GMT the lat was 20 points below its strongest \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level on the bid side, versus 15 at Thursday's \par \par \uc2  open. It was 36 points stronger than parity on the offer side. \par \par \uc2  The lat has stuck to a range of 15-20 points off its \par \par \uc2  strongest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level this week, buoyed by a strong \par \par \uc2  dollar, which creates demand for cheap lats on the local market. \par \par \uc2  "There is no direction. It is just staying where it is," \par \par \uc2  said Unibanka dealer Kristaps Strazds. \par \par \uc2  Dealers have been expecting a lat slide for weeks but the \par \par \uc2  dollar's strength has made it reluctant to give up its gains of \par \par \uc2  recent months on the back of government bond issues and \par \par \uc2  privatisations. \par \par \uc2  "The prognosis is still the same. Most probably we will not \par \par \uc2  see \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2  as there is usually quite \par \par \uc2  active demand for \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the lat reaches within 10 \par \par \uc2  points of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Strazds said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say the lat will eventually find a lower resistence \par \par \uc2  level around parity, but it will take its time getting there. \par \par \uc2  The market's dollar rate was 0.6068/73 against the lat, \par \par \uc2  versus 0.6076/81 early on Thursday, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \par \par \uc2  rate was 0.6048/170, where it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  within its two percent SDR band. \par \par \uc2  The lat is pegged at 0.7997 to the IMF's SDR world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  basket - which includes the dollar, the yen and other major \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It fluctuates in a band of one percent either side. \par \par \uc2  (( Burton Frierson, Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240, fax +371 \par \par \uc2  724 3139, reuters@reuters.lv )). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw5c00l0c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
