\par\par \b \uc2  Latvian 6mo T-bill yields,money mkt rates seen down. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Burton Frierson \par \uc2 566 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Mai 2000\par 17:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  RIGA, May 5 (Reuters) - Latvian government debt yields and money market rates look set to soften further next week in line with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's aim to see lower rates, analysts said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The market also expects the lat to cede some more of its recent gains. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said stocks lack the impetus to move forward next week after the state failed sell five percent stake in oil terminal Ventspils Nafta  on April 28. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday the finance ministry will sell two million lats ($3.2 million) of six-month T-bills. Their average yield fell to 5.0 percent on April 26 from 5.79 percent before. \par \par \uc2  "I expected something around 4.5 percent as the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  (on the secondary market) at about 3.5 percent," said Hansabanka dealer Elmars Priksans. \par \par \uc2  "Definitely banks would speculate on that and try to sell them to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  later," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the money market was still indifferent to political developments, even with parliament expected to vote in a new government being formed by Prime Minister-designate Andris Berzins at 1500 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said only a decision by Berzins' majority government to depart from the outgoing cabinet's tight fiscal policy could affect market sentiment, which seems unlikely based on the government declaration agreed this week. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday the finance ministry will also auction 700,000 lats of three-month paper and 500,000 lats of one-month bills. \par \par \uc2  The last rates at auction were 3.84 percent on three-month and 3.37 percent on one-month bills. Dealers say the paper is nearing bottom but could still have some room to slide. \par \par \uc2  On the interbank lending market, average bids on overnight money     rose 77 percent over the week to 1.38 percent with the start of a new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve requirment period. However, they fell 46 percent versus this time last month. \par \par \uc2  "Money market rates probably will go a bit lower as liquidity on the market is high," said Priksans. \par \par \uc2  On the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market dealers expected the lat to move off recent highs next week after easing back off the strongest levels in its trading band this week. \par \par \uc2  "I think the trend is for the lat to weaken, but slowly. It looks like banks have more interest to buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  than sell," said Andrejs Greivulis, a dealer at Vereinsbank Riga. \par \par \uc2  At 1428 GMT the lat was 15 points off its strongest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level, versus 17 at the start of trade. \par \par \uc2  Dealers have been expecting the lat to slide back in the direction of parity within its trading bank for weeks but say the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has held tightly to its gains of the last two months on the back of government bond issues and privatisations. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Ventspils Nafta  would remain the focus of share trade next week, as the market puzzles over how to handle its privatisation. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The stock fell 8.3 percent to 0.77 lats over the week as the main index \tab   slid seven percent to 172.58, a 17-week low.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers expect most of the market to be lacklustre amid a lack of corporate news and interesting new issues.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Riga Newsroom +371 722 2079, fax +371 724 3139, reuters@reuters.lv)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw5501vso\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
