\par\par \b \uc2  Latvian cbank says  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  eased last week. \b0\par\par\uc2 260 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 1999\par 10:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  RIGA, Sept 21 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday it sold about $5 million on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the lat last week versus about $8 million the previous week. \par \par \uc2  "About $5 million last week...in September $25 million. Those are just ballpark figures," Arvids Sipols, deputy head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Latvia's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  department, told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began an almost daily spate of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in July when nagging worries about a gaping budget deficit combined with intermittent dollar bargain hunting to weaken the lat \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In the last two weeks demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has tapered off, helped by a dollar rise against the yen last week and a jump in interbank interest rates, which rose amid the general lat drain in the past two months. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell 5.4 percent to 644.3 million lats in August due to the demand for dollars as well as the closing of swap positions. \par \par \uc2  The lat is pegged at 0.7997 lats to the IMF's SDR world basket \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - which includes the dollar, the yen and other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It is allowed to fluctuate in a band of one percent either side. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not usually enter the market when the lat is safely within the band but steps in more or less automatically when it threatens to leave. \par \par \uc2  ((Burton Frierson, Riga newsroom, +371 722 7029, reuters@reuters.lv)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9l00cb2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
