\par\par \b \uc2  Latvian c.bank says  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  eased last week. \b0\par\par\uc2 301 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 1999\par 11:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  RIGA, Sept 14 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday it had sold just $8 million last week in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the lat \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after selling $30 million the week before. \par \par \uc2  "We sold approximately $8 million last week...now actually we have been out of the market for one week already," Andrejs Viks, portfolio manager at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on an almost daily basis in July as the lat slid against the SDR basket amid budget deficit worries. Intermittent bargain hunting for the dollar exacerbated the Latvian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakness. \par \par \uc2  It said on Monday \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell 5.4 percent in August to 644.3 million lats ($1.103 billion) due to demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the closing of swap positions. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand turned to appetite for the Latvian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week as market players moved to take advantage of higher interbank rates brought on by the general lat drain. \par \par \uc2  The lat was off the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels lat last week and on Monday but seemed to be easing back on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  At 0931 the market's offered dollar rate was 0.5894 against the lat while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate, which is the level at which it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was 0.5895. \par \par \uc2  The lat is pegged at 0.7997 lats to the SDR, the IMF's world basket \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and is allowed to fluctuate in a band of one percent either side. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not usually enter the market when the lat is safely within the band but steps in more or less automatically when it threatens to leave. \par \par \uc2  ((Burton Frierson, Riga newsroom +371 722 2079, reuters@reuters.lv)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9e00o6d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
