\par\par \b \uc2  Latvian cbank says Aug  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  around $40 mln. \b0\par\par\uc2 423 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 1999\par 14:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  RIGA, Aug 30 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold around $40 million while \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market so far in August, as the lat \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sagged amid worries over the budget deficit, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Arvids Sipols, deputy head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  department, also told Reuters that the bank had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "Around $40 million for the month. Those are rounded figures and they will of course show up on the balance sheet quarterly reports," Sipols said. \par \par \uc2  "I guess the psychological environment is not so healthy so we've been hitting the market rates, so we are doing something in the market (today)," he added. \par \par \uc2  Sipols said the central had sold about $20 million during \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week and $18 million the week before. \par \par \uc2  He declined to comment on the size of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday since the bank usually does not discuss how much it buys or sells on a daily basis. \par \par \uc2  At 1239 GMT the market's offered dollar rate was 0.5931 against the lat while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate, which is its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, was 0.5932. \par \par \uc2  The lat has remained weak since last month after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time this year amid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  worries originally sparked by a gaping budget deficit. \par \par \uc2  Parliament earlier this month passed a package of 27.95 million lats worth of spending cuts to the 1999 budget but they were less than half the amount recommended by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the government will have to find more ways to reduce spending this year since the fiscal deficit is expected to reach 3.5 percent of GDP as the budget stands now. \par \par \uc2  Intermittent dollar weakness abroad has further hurt already weak lat sentiment due to bargain hunting for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Recent local media reports of comments by Ventspils Mayor Aivars Lembergs - who had said he was moving municipal funds into dollars due to lat worries - also hit retail-level sentiment. \par \par \uc2  The lat is pegged at 0.7997 lats to the SDR, the IMF's world basket \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and is allowed to fluctuate in a band of one percent either side. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not usually enter the market when the lat is safely within the band but steps in more or less automatically when it threatens to leave. \par \par \uc2  ((Burton Frierson, Riga Newsroom +371 722 2079, reuters@reuters.lv)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8u01q0v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
