\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS- \highlight22\uc2 Latvia \highlight\uc2  sells $40mln in August  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Alan Crosby \par \uc2 562 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 1999\par 16:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  RIGA, Aug 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to boost the sagging lat \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday, continuing a spate of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in which it said it sold $40 million this month amid pension and budget deficit worries. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 1350 GMT the market's offered dollar rate\tab   was 0.5932 against the lat while the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rate, which is its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate, was also 0.5932\tab  .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  The lat has been weak for the past month since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time this year amid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  worries originally sparked by a gaping budget deficit. This month it said it had sold $40 million during \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Around $40 million for the month. Those are rounded figures and they will of course show up on the balance sheet quarterly reports," said Arvids Sipols, deputy head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  department. \par \par \uc2  "I guess the psychological environment is not so healthy so we've been hitting the market rates, so we are doing something in the market (today)," he added. \par \par \uc2  At the end of July \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  foreign reserves stood at 681.3 million lats, after falling 13.3 million lats that month. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they were not worried by the size of August's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves looked good for now. \par \par \uc2  "If it (the rate of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) continued for three, four or five months, that could become a bit dangerous for lat stability...(but) of course the market is waiting for some bigger budget cuts," the dealer added. \par \par \uc2  Earlier this month parliament approved 27.95 million lats in cuts to the 1999 budget, less than half the amount recommended by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A fiscal deficit of 3.5 percent of GDP is still expected as the budget stands now. \par \par \uc2  Intermittent dollar weakness abroad has further hurt already weak lat sentiment due to bargain hunting for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Recent comments by Ventspils Mayor Aivars Lembergs - who said he was moving municipal funds into dollars due to lat worries - also hit retail sentiment. \par \par \uc2  Adding further to the lat's problems in recent days has been the issue of pension reform. \par \par \uc2  Parliament earlier this month, along with the 1999 spending cuts, approved pension amendments to shore up next year's budget, but the opposition managed to block implementation. \par \par \uc2  Supporters of a referendum now have until October 5 to collect 134,000 signatures to force a poll which could overturn the deputies' vote. \par \par \uc2  A Latvian finance ministry spokeswoman said on Monday Minister Edmunds Krastinsh believes a failure to cut spending on pensions will threaten the long-term stability of the lat. "He connects this with the overall economic situation in Latvia and problems with the social budget, which may lead to further borrowing that may, later, prompt a devaluation of the lat," spokeswoman Baiba Melnace told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The lat is pegged at 0.7997 lats to the SDR, the IMF's world basket \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and is allowed to fluctuate in a band of one percent either side. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not usually enter the market when the lat is safely within the band but steps in more or less automatically when it threatens to leave. \par \par \uc2  ((Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240, fax: +371 724 3139, reuters@reuters.lv)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8u01dsk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
