\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Latvian 7-mo budget deficit 73.89 mln lats. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Burton Frierson \par \uc2 493 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 1999\par 17:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  RIGA, Aug 26 (Reuters) - Latvia said on Thursday the budget deficit continued to rise in July, and dealers expected the news to keep an already weak lat \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  soft but did not see it causing major new ripples on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Latvia's consolidated state budget deficit for the first seven months of the year was 73.89 million lats, a rise from 67.281 million lats after the first half of 1999, the finance ministry said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Edmunds Krastinsh also told a news conference that the first sign of any improvement in tax revenues - which have slumped under the weight of last year's Russian crisis - would appear in October at the earliest. \par \par \uc2  "We will see first in October if the positive signs we have seen in the economy indeed signify a recovery after the Russian crisis," Krastinsh told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  Retail-level worries over the gaping fiscal deficit forced the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time this year to support the lat after six-month budget deficit figures were announced. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say it has been on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on an almost daily basis ever since, although volumes are small and foreign positions have yet to emerge against the lat. \par \par \uc2  Intermittent dollar weakness abroad has further hurt already weak lat sentiment due to bargain hunting for the U.S. unit, but the budget has been the main focus, dealers say. \par \par \uc2  Latvia's budget deficit is expected to reach 3.5 percent of GDP this year, even after a 27.95 million lat package of spending cuts approved by parliament earlier this month. \par \par \uc2  The cuts were less than half what the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had recommeded. \par \par \uc2  The World Bank's country director for Poland and the Baltic states, Basil Kavalsky, last week joined a chorus of analysts calling for further cuts, telling Reuters in an interview it was "the key to the stability of the lat". \par \par \uc2  "I think more fiscal tightening is needed," said Leonid Ruderman, head trader at local Parex Bank. \par \par \uc2  However, Ruderman did not expect Thursday's news about the deficit to affect \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) selling dollars all this week. The lat can't weaken any further," Ruderman said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserve position remained strong going into August - despite July's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - and the government is still flush with funds after selling a 150 million euro bond in May. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not face any additional pressure (due to the budget deficit news)," said Martinsh Jaunarajs, short-term liquidity manager with Hansabana. \par \par \uc2  "This won't create a new wave of dollar buyers but this (negative) sentiment on the retail level will keep on for some time," Jaunarajs added. \par \par \uc2  ((Riga Newsroom +371 722 2079, riga.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8q01t9o\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\b